    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d830">

                <pb facs="0829" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1740b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d830-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 13, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2272. Reported British authorities have notified transatlantic steamship
                    companies that future shipments foodstuffs from the United States will be seized
                    unless before acceptance [of] such shipments, companies report to London names
                    consignor and consignee, and description goods, and obtain permission to carry
                    shipments. Investigate thoroughly and telegraph report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d830-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d830-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Minister in Denmark, No. 43, October 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
